---
// One-line "what this tab does" explainer, rendered at the top of a dashboard panel.
//
// Shown ONLY while the seller's onboarding checklist is still incomplete (the parent decides) —
// so a first-time seller is told what every tab is for, and an established seller never carries
// the extra line. Same derived signal as the checklist, so nothing is stored or dismissed.
//
// **A line of text, and deliberately nothing more** (owner, 2026-08-24, after six attempts at
// making it a box: *"פשוט לפני כל השינויים… הכי פשוט"*). It was tried as the sheet's own top band,
// nested inside its border, pinned, tucked a radius behind the container below, and finally as a
// small card of its own — and each one produced one more visible box on a screen that already has
// two. The reason is structural rather than aesthetic: this element lives INSIDE `.dash-panel`,
// whose side borders wrap whatever is in it, so a bordered box here is always a box inside a box.
// A container ABOVE the sheet would have to be a SIBLING of it, which means moving this out of the
// panel in `dashboard.astro` — a real change, not a CSS one, and worth doing only if the box is
// wanted for its own sake. Until then: `--color-muted`, an icon, one line.
interface Props {
  text: string;
}
const { text } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="flex items-start gap-[0.4rem] m-0 mb-3 text-[0.82rem] leading-[1.5] [color:var(--color-muted)]">
  <svg class="shrink-0 mt-[0.15rem]" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"/>
  </svg>
  <span>{text}</span>
</p>
